Faceplate controls
------------------

dm/faceplate.h provides the classic in-view menu and slider drawing and hit
testing, extracted from MGED. A dm_faceplate_controls provider enumerates rows
and receives selections. The application retains its editing state, units,
command interpreter and database knowledge. An optional label renderer can
highlight application-specific modes without adding those modes to libdm.

dm_set_faceplate_gui registers a borrowed description on a display manager;
dm_draw_faceplate draws it alongside the existing bv overlays. Registration
is optional and disabled by default. Applications drawing their own HUD can
instead call dm_faceplate_controls_draw and dm_faceplate_controls_select
directly, as MGED does to retain its historical placement of edit information.
Use matching normalized HUD coordinates for drawing and input. Hidden rows
are excluded from both drawing and selection.
